# SalesView project rules

## Design system
- Main background: `#F1F5F9`
- Card background: `#FFFFFF`
- Primary color: `#1E3A5F`
- Positive metric: `#10B981`
- Negative metric: `#EF4444`
- Text primary: `#0F172A`
- Text secondary: `#64748B`
- Borders and separators: `#E2E8F0`
- Category colors:
  - Electronica: `#3B82F6`
  - Ropa: `#8B5CF6`
  - Hogar: `#F59E0B`
  - Alimentos: `#10B981`
  - Deportes: `#EF4444`

## Component structure
- Keep each React component in its own file under `src/components/`.
- Use `src/App.jsx` only as the composition layer for dashboard sections and data derivation.
- Keep shared formatting and aggregation helpers in `src/utils.js`.

## Data source
- All data is mock data stored in local JSON files under `data/`.
- Do not add API calls, backend integration, authentication, or persistence.
- `data/sales.json` stores transactions, `data/team.json` stores sellers, and `data/config.json` stores global dashboard config.

## Product constraints
- Keep the app as a single-page dashboard without routing.
- Do not add dark mode, login, editing flows, notifications, tooltips, popovers, PDF/Excel export, or real-time updates.
- Do not add chart libraries; progress and category bars must remain CSS-based.
- Keep the experience read-only and focused on fast executive scanning.
